      "problem": "$\\frac{1}{5}÷7=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $7$ is $\\frac{1}{7}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,÷\\,7=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{1\\times 1}{5\\times 7}=\\frac{1}{35}\n$$",
